  "description": "Production-grade Firebase Cloud Messaging (push notifications) for .NET: automatic batching over FCM's 500-token limit, dead-token reporting, topic broadcast, retry with backoff, explicit fail-open behaviour, and an optional built-in device-token store (generic-key, provider-neutral, self-migrating) that owns the FirebaseUserDevices table, prunes dead tokens, keeps an in-app inbox, and audits every send.",
  "id": "AQZ.Firebase.Toolkit",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-20T14:16:41.323Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "bT51jbL6h+ORY/tXXQNE+nH2N9YEfnx3PVb+WOIb39vvZyrUINoUWaEbzxMzxWAgs0MHJmEStJWaNpjjn9ZVkA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 83707,
  "published": "2026-11-20T14:07:28.75Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "3.7.0: Upgraded Microsoft.Extensions.* and Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational from 10.0.0 to 10.0.15 to align with consuming apps and fix EF Core version conflicts when running migrations. No API change, no schema change, no migration; non-breaking. 3.6.0: IUserPushService gains a BroadcastAsync overload that excludes a caller-supplied set of user ids (BroadcastAsync(message, excludeUserIds, ct)), so a consuming app can honour a per-user notification preference on broadcast without the toolkit knowing what a preference is. Backed by a new repository query (GetActiveTokensPagedExcludingUsersAsync). No schema change, no migration; non-breaking. 3.5.0: the send audit gains a first-class Category (event-type) column on FirebaseNotificationDispatches, populated from the message data key (FirebaseStoreOptions.CategoryDataKey, default \"category\") and filterable via NotificationDispatchQuery.Category, so admin history can be filtered by event type without parsing JSON. Adds a column + index: generate one store migration after upgrading. Non-breaking. 3.4.0: complete send auditing across all audiences (Users, Broadcast, Tokens, Topic, Condition) into FirebaseNotificationDispatches. 3.3.0: data/options types unsealed for inheritance.",
